        <outline title="The John Batchelor Show" text="The John Batchelor Show is a hard news-analysis radio program on current events, world history, global politics and natural sciences. Based in New York City for two decades, the show has travelled widely to report, from the Middle East to the South Caucasus to the Arabian Peninsula and East Asia." xmlUrl="https://www.spreaker.com/show/7297166/episodes/feed" type="rss"/>
        <outline title="Team Human" text="&lt;p&gt;Douglas Rushkoff sits down with scientists, activists, artists, philosophers, and researchers asking the same question: who actually benefits from the way we&amp;#39;ve built this world — and what do we do about it? Team Human is a weekly podcast about technology, power, consciousness, and what it means to stay human in a world that increasingly doesn&amp;#39;t seem designed for us. No corporate backing. No network. No algorithm deciding what gets said. Just honest, rigorous conversation with people working at the edges of the most important questions of our time. &lt;/p&gt;" xmlUrl="https://feeds.redcircle.com/3d87dea6-3d7d-4d94-b02e-9eb931541da8" type="rss"/>
        <outline title="Green News Report w/ Brad Friedman &amp; Desi Doyen" text="Six minutes of nationally-syndicated independent green news, politics, analysis and snarky comment!" xmlUrl="https://bradblog.com/podcastgen/GNR/feed.xml" type="rss"/>
        <outline title="The Next System Podcast" text="The Next System Podcast is a regular series that examines the systemic challenges facing society today and the bold, systemic solutions that can build the society of tomorrow. Learn more about the Next System Project at www.thenextsystem.org." xmlUrl="https://nextsystem.libsyn.com/rss" type="rss"/>
        <outline title="News Beat" text="A social justice podcast combining hard-hitting journalism and interviews with hip-hop music and original lyrics from independent artists. Each episode delves into an important issue with an alternative take to widely accepted narratives, arming listeners with knowledge and insight they won't hear from mainstream media outlets." xmlUrl="https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/ed1c4567-4a2a-4d8b-862f-ab600003d530/24e95e5d-204a-4bdf-bbf8-ab6f016788ff/9b234dab-0449-442c-9203-ab6f01678903/podcast.rss" type="rss"/>
